YMXS License
============

YMXS is the tune data structure for the Atari ST's YM2149 and MC68901, and
what a player does with it. This repository contains the specification
(the records under src/main/java/org/ymxs, and doc/SPEC.md), the two forms
(doc/json.md and doc/csv.md), the five tools in Java under src/ and in Go
under go/, a reader of YM register dumps, and the tests.

The format may be implemented freely. doc/SPEC.md is the contract, and an
independent reader, player or writer owes only the acknowledgement below.

1. THE DOCUMENTS under doc/ and this file are Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert
   van Dalen.

2. THE STRUCTURE, TOOLS AND TESTS can be used freely within your programs,
   for any platform, even for commercial releases. The only condition is
   that you must indicate somehow in your documentation that you have
   used YMXS. They are everything under src/, go/, bin/ and release/, and
   the executables the releases carry.

   The tunes under doc/tunes are example input, and the music in them is
   outside this licence.

Attribution
-----------

* YMXS, its specification, its tools and its tests are Copyright (c) 2026
  Robbert van Dalen; written by Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code) under
  Robbert van Dalen's direction.
* The YM5 and YM6 register-dump formats are by Arnaud Carré
  (Leonard/Oxygene); src/main/java/org/ymxs/ym and go/ym read them.
* The LHA depacker in src/main/java/org/ymxs/ym/Lha.java and go/ym/lha.go
  is a port of StSoundLibrary/LZH/LzhLib.cpp from ST-Sound by Arnaud
  Carré, itself based on LZH code by Haruhiko Okumura (1991) and Kerwin F.
  Medina (1996). It carries both notices below.
* The 68000's cost of entering an interrupt and leaving it, 44 and 20
  cycles, which bounds the rate a timer may run at, is from Motorola's
  manual.

Used by the build and the tests, not distributed
------------------------------------------------

* Maven pulls Jackson, JSpecify, JUnit, Error Prone and NullAway for the
  Java build, and the Go toolchain builds go/. No copy of any of them is
  kept here.

ST-Sound notices (the LHA depacker)
-----------------------------------

The LHA depacker in src/main/java/org/ymxs/ym/Lha.java and go/ym/lha.go is a
port of StSoundLibrary/LZH/LzhLib.cpp from ST-Sound, which carries both
notices below.

